  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.542) is the best so far, and the progression from config_001→004→031 shows that weighted fusion > concat and imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, both with scgpt and multiprofile. The one untested dimension within this best-performing family is the aggregation method (avgpool vs. transformer). This experiment tests whether transformer aggregation can further improve accuracy by better modeling inter-profile relationships, while keeping all other parameters at their empirically best values. It is the highest-value next step because it directly extends the strongest configuration along the most impactful unexplored axis, and with 6 experiments remaining we can still probe RNA-encoder alternatives (scvi_n200, pca_n2000) and profile-setting (singleprofile) in later runs. Expected cost: transformer aggregation over multiple profiles adds attention computation, so I estimate ~4.5–5.5 GPU hours, somewhat higher than config_031's 2.94 but still within budget (total would be ~17–18 GPU hours after this experiment)."
}

